# A builtin called with too FEW arguments. tychoc has arity from its Sig table
# (register_builtins, src/tychoc.c:4176-4207, checked at :5548-5550); tychoc0 had
# none, so `substr` walked off the end of its own args array and died with
# "tycho: index 2 out of bounds (len 1)" -- an internal message, no source line.
# Both must now reject with a located arity diagnostic.

fn main():
    println(substr("hi"))
